      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided",
      "description": "Scope and content:  Original Caption: Alter at New York Public Library.  Wreath commemorating dead of 27th Division laying in front of the Public Library, placed by men of 27th Division who brought it there on a gun caisson during the big parade.  Crowds unable to reach this part of the city during the parade admiring the wonderful decorations.  Above the wreath is a list of battles the 27th Division fought in.\nPhotographer: Western Newspaper Union",
